# Project Rules: __PROJECT_NAME__

> Updated on: __DATE__

These rules turn document-driven development from a suggestion into the default working mode.

## Rule Guide

### Before implementation

- `docs/rules/clarification-rules.md`: requirement clarification, material ambiguity, and user confirmation rules
- `docs/rules/document-routing-rules.md`: semantic-to-path routing rules

### During implementation

- `docs/rules/coding-standards.md`: coding rules, comments, and implementation boundaries
- `docs/rules/testing-standards.md`: test layers, regression rules, and quality gates
- `docs/rules/bug-fix-rules.md`: root-cause bug fixing and regression rules

### Documentation sync and change governance

- `docs/rules/doc-sync-rules.md`: sync rules for code, tests, current-state docs, and long-lived knowledge
- `docs/rules/change-management-rules.md`: change workspace, lifecycle, and historical record rules
- `docs/rules/document-archive-rules.md`: record document IDs, indexes, and year/month archive rules
- `docs/rules/issue-management-rules.md`: issue, risk, technical debt, and retired document rules

### Commit, review, and completion

- `docs/rules/commit-rules.md`: commit format, document links, scope, and test status rules
- `docs/rules/definition-of-done.md`: completion checklist

## How to use this directory

1. Read this directory before implementation starts
2. When a trade-off appears, check whether a default rule already exists here
3. Run analyze before implementation to confirm requirements, design, verification, tasks, and the change workspace do not conflict
4. Run converge after implementation to update current docs, long-lived truth, and change history
5. Before committing, read `docs/rules/commit-rules.md` and ensure the commit body includes links, scope, impact, and test status
6. As the project evolves, add new rules here instead of leaving them in chat or PR comments only
